This program is designed to analyze the performance of multiple students based on their marks. 
It begins by asking the user to enter the total number of students and then stores each student’s mark in a one-dimensional array.
Using loops, it calculates the total sum of marks to determine the average score. It also checks each mark to identify the highest and lowest values.
The program classifies each student as passed or failed based on a minimum passing mark of 50. Additionally, it assigns grades (A+, A, B, C, D, or Fail) according to predefined mark ranges and counts how many students fall into each grade category
Finally, it displays a detailed summary including the average mark, highest and lowest marks, number of passed and failed students, and the overall grade distribution.
